<title>USA: Harrington initiates qtly div at $0.03/shr.</title>
<headline>Harrington initiates qtly div at $0.03/shr.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Ind. 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harrington Financial Group said Monday that it was initiating a quarterly dividend of $0.03 per share, reflecting the company's level of profitability and its  shareholders preference for dividends.</p>
<p>The company said the dividend will be payable May 30 to shareholders of record May 15.</p>
<p>Harrington is a thrift-holding company with $515.4 million in assets.</p>
</text>
